cs.t:
I switched to System76 last year from being on a mac for about 15 years. I knew that there would be some things which would be lower quality (speakers, webcam, mic, trackpad, screen) but found a couple of things: 1/ my machine is way faster and lasts way longer;
2/ I have had really great support from System76 (esp. compared to Apple -- they helped me debug a hardware problem and then I just ordered a new card and popped it in myself);
3/ I actually don't mind the quality degradation compared to the massive improvement in my day-to-day experience. I'm an Arch user (/fanatic -- aren't we all?), YMMV.
